WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:05.880
So in the bottom we see neon and this is a
small glass discharge tube

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:10.270
which has got a very low pressure of neon
inside it. It’s generally used

00:00:10.270 --> 00:00:13.440
for lots of signs and things like that. You
might see ‘Fish and Chips’ or

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:16.059
perhaps a ‘disco’ or something like that.

00:00:16.059 --> 00:00:24.840
So Neon is an inert gas like helium and it
doesn’t really form any

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:29.970
compounds at all. Most of you have probably
seen neon because it’s

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:34.760
used in these so-called neon signs where you
take a glass tube and put a

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:38.479
high voltage and it produces a red light.

00:00:38.479 --> 00:00:42.200
So you can see that, again, a discharge, a
high potential discharge is

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:46.170
going across this tube and it’s exciting
all of the neon molecules inside,

00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:49.539
such that we get this exciting, really vivid
red colouration.

00:00:49.539 --> 00:00:54.909
And skilled glass-blowers can blow this into
glass shapes of signs saying

00:00:54.909 --> 00:01:00.699
‘pizza’ or whatever on shops. You can
freeze neon at very low

00:01:00.699 --> 00:01:06.190
temperatures about 10 degrees absolute and
early on in my scientific

00:01:06.190 --> 00:01:10.900
career I did do an experiment in solid neon.
It produced a great result

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:14.970
with an iron compound and I’m still quite
proud of it several years on.

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:22.100
But it’s not really very important in terms
of absolute chemistry.

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:26.780
So this is just a simple pocket spectroscope
and it allows us to analyse

00:01:26.780 --> 00:01:30.380
the wavelengths of light that each of these
individual light sources is

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:35.860
giving off. So each individual atom as it’s
excited in its emission zone can

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:39.251
give rise to different lines or different
frequencies of radiation or light

00:01:39.251 --> 00:01:42.740
and we can use this little device to analyse
which elements are in each

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:45.520
of these different elements of light. So we
put it up to our eyes and we

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:50.030
look through, and we look at the different
colours of the lines in the

00:01:50.030 --> 00:01:50.810
different gases.

